            <ArticleTitle>Fatal case of imported human rabies in Amadora, Portugal, August 2011.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">20130</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of imported human rabies in Portugal, in July 2011 in a woman who presented initially complaining of back pain, without relating exposure to animal bites. She had travelled from Portugal to Bissau, Guinea-Bissau, in April where she had been bitten by a dog on 1 May. She was diagnosed with rabies on 26 July and died two weeks later in spite of being treated following the Milwaukee protocol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
